<title>MEXICO: RESEARCH ALERT - Gidusa lowered.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Gidusa lowered.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Caspian analysts Jorge Beristain and Sebastien Chatel said on Wednesday they downgraded their rating on Grupo Industrial Durango (Gidusa) to market performer from buy, citing its &quot;recent strong price performance.&quot;</p>
<p>In a report, the analysts added that the company's operating outlook looked positive, and the second half should benefit from plant expansions.</p>
<p>The paper product company's shares were at 63.40 pesos, unchanged from Tuesday's closing price.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
</text>
